## Rationale
shiva_db.py was using sqlite3.connect() directly to write to shiva_memory/shiva.db. This file lives outside the artifacts directory and was never migrated. All production writes must go through get_connection() → Postgres. This change routes Shiva's journal sessions and nodes to sweet_pea_rudi19.shiva_journal_sessions and shiva_nodes tables.

## Risk Assessment
  Risk Level: LOW
  Reversible: YES — SQLite file still exists as fallback reference
  Dependencies: core.db.get_connection() must be importable from agents/shiva/ context (sys.path must include Willow root). WILLOW_DB_URL must be set in environment.
  Note: Table names change from journal_sessions/nodes to shiva_journal_sessions/shiva_nodes. init_db() will create these tables in sweet_pea_rudi19 schema on first run.
